course: dictionary
lesson: 16046
title: Vietnamese: one word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vietnamese can change its job in a sentence, and the words around it show which job it has. «We ate Vietnamese spring rolls at the party.» Here Vietnamese describes the food, telling us the spring rolls came from Vietnam.
explain: «Mai is Vietnamese, and her family moved to Sydney.» Here Vietnamese names a person from Vietnam, or someone of Vietnamese family.
explain: «At home, Mai's grandma speaks Vietnamese.» Here Vietnamese names a language. Whatever its job, Vietnamese always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Vietnam is a country in South-East Asia.
fact: «Vietnamese» is an adjective when it describes something, like «Vietnamese food».
fact: «Vietnamese» is a noun when it means a person from Vietnam, or the language spoken there.
fact: Vietnamese is written with the Latin alphabet, plus many accent marks, and it has tones.
fact: Pho and spring rolls are Vietnamese food, and many Vietnamese families live in Australia, the USA, Canada and the UK.
exercise: «We ate Vietnamese spring rolls at the party.» What does Vietnamese tell us about the spring rolls? | *Where they come from: Vietnam | What colour they were | How many there were | Who made them
exercise: Mai says, «I am Vietnamese.» What does Vietnamese mean here? | The language spoken in Vietnam | A type of bird | A kind of soup | *A person from Vietnam, or of Vietnamese family
exercise: Vietnam is a country in which part of the world? | South America | Africa | Europe | *South-East Asia
test: «Grandma speaks Vietnamese at home.» What is Vietnamese in this sentence? | A colour | The name of a food | A sport | *The name of a language
test: Which fact about Vietnamese writing is true? | It uses only numbers | It uses no letters at all | *It uses the Latin alphabet with extra accent marks | It is written with pictures only
exam: Ben says, «Vietnamese food is tasty.» What kind of word is Vietnamese here? | A noun for a person | *An adjective | A noun for a language | A verb
